          "cells": [
            "Sequencing Whole-exome sequencing: Genomic DNA is enriched using oligonucleotide probes complementary to portions of the genome encoding proteins. Sequencing only the coding portion of the genome focuses the effort to 1–2% of the genome and is more cost-effective, requiring the generation of only 6–9 billion bases of sequence. Whole-genome sequencing: Unbiased sequencing of the whole genome. In the context of cancer genome sequencing, this requires the generation of 90–180 billion bases from the tumor and 90 billion bases from the patient's normal DNA."
